cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "agent-containment-replay"
message: "If you use this corpus or the frozen detector, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alkur"
    given-names: "Jaswanth"
    email: "lathajaswanth7@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alkur123/agent-containment-replay"
abstract: >
  Replayable agent trajectories reconstructed from the frontier-lab
  evaluation-containment failures disclosed in July and August 2026, together
  with a dependency-free scorer, an example monitor, and two public
  pre-registrations. The registrations fix a hash-pinned detector, a threshold
  and a segmentation specification in advance of the transcripts they are
  written against, so a later result can be scored without the analysis choices
  being made with the data open. The corpus is small and its limitations are
  stated in the README rather than in a footnote: the fixtures are narrated
  decision points rather than complete action logs, and the detector was built
  on material of the same kind it is scored against.
keywords:
  - "ai-safety"
  - "ai-control"
  - "ai-agents"
  - "agent-monitoring"
  - "red-teaming"
  - "pre-registration"
  - "reproducibility"
license: "MIT"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
